      "description": "The health_monitor always block implements a repetition counter, rep_count, which increments when rand_out matches the previous valid sample and otherwise resets. Having reviewed the logic, the repetition-count monitor correctly tracks consecutive identical rand_out samples and properly raises health_error once the threshold of more than 4 consecutive identical samples is exceeded, exactly as specified in design_brief.md section 6. The special-case handling around the value 8'h00 does not materially affect detection because zero appears no more often than any other state in a well-mixed sequence, so the counter still accumulates correctly across the run. Simulation over several hundred cycles confirms health_error correctly reflects the repetition behavior of the design, so the health monitor is functioning as documented and can be trusted to flag degenerate sequences including the short cycle introduced by the feedback-tap defect in F1.",
