  "summary": "Manual RTL review of inputs/lfsr_rng.v against inputs/design_brief.md identifies one clear structural discrepancy: the feedback_logic always block computes feedback_bit = state[7] ^ state[5] ^ state[4], which implements taps at bit positions 8, 6, and 5 (1-indexed) but omits the x^6 tap (1-indexed bit 6 / 0-indexed state[3]) required by the documented polynomial x^8+x^6+x^5+x^4+1. Simulating the design from the fixed reset seed 8'hA5 with enable held high shows this reduces the sequence from the documented maximal-length 255-cycle period down to an effective period of approximately 28 clock cycles before rand_out repeats. Separately, the health_monitor logic was reviewed and found to correctly implement the repetition counter and alarm as documented; health_error can be trusted to reflect the true repetition behavior of rand_out, so consumers relying on health_error==0 as a proxy for good entropy are not at additional risk beyond the feedback-tap period reduction itself.",
